I have everything needed. Here is a thorough report of the current owner duplicate-detection implementation.

## Overview

Duplicate detection runs only on the **POST /api/owners** (create) path, wired as OfficeFloor functions. The **PUT** (update) path does NOT run any duplicate checks. There are three independent checks — telephone, email, household (lastName + address) — each with its own exception + handler, all returning HTTP 409. There is currently **no unified `identityKey`** concept; the acceptance test's top comment signals that consolidation into a derived `identityKey` is the intended change.

---

## 1. Duplicate-detection functions

### /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CheckTelephoneUnique.java
Compares E.164-normalized telephone against every existing owner.
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateTelephoneException {
    String telephone = normalize(request.getTelephone());
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (telephone.equals(normalize(existing.getTelephone()))) {
            throw new DuplicateTelephoneException(request.getTelephone());
        }
    }
}
private static String normalize(String telephone) {
    String e164 = TelephoneE164.normalize(telephone);
    return e164 == null ? "" : e164;
}
```

### /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CheckEmailUnique.java
Compares trimmed/lower-cased email; skips when email absent/blank.
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateEmailException {
    String email = normalize(request.getEmail());
    if (email.isEmpty()) {
        return;
    }
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (email.equals(normalize(existing.getEmail()))) {
            throw new DuplicateEmailException(request.getEmail());
        }
    }
}
private static String normalize(String value) {
    if (value == null) {
        return "";
    }
    return value.trim().toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
}
```

### /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/CheckHouseholdUnique.java
Rejects same normalized lastName + normalized address, unless `sharesHousehold: true`.
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, OwnerRepository ownerRepository)
        throws DuplicateHouseholdException {
    if (Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
        return;
    }
    String lastName = normalize(request.getLastName());
    String address = AddressNormalizer.normalize(request.getAddress());
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (lastName.equals(normalize(existing.getLastName()))
                && address.equals(AddressNormalizer.normalize(existing.getAddress()))) {
            throw new DuplicateHouseholdException(request.getLastName(), request.getAddress());
        }
    }
}
private static String normalize(String value) {
    if (value == null) {
        return "";
    }
    return value.trim().replaceAll("\\s+", " ").toLowerCase(Locale.ROOT);
}
```

### /home/daniel/sandbox/src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/function/owner/AssignHousehold.java
Runs after build; when `sharesHousehold: true`, derives a stable `householdId = first 16 upper-hex chars of SHA-256(normalizedLastName + "|" + normalizedAddress)` and stamps it on the new owner plus every existing same-household owner. Full method bodies:
```java
public void service(@Val OwnerFieldsDto request, @Val Owner owner, OwnerRepository ownerRepository) {
    if (!Boolean.TRUE.equals(request.getSharesHousehold())) {
        return;
    }
    String lastName = normalize(owner.getLastName());
    String address = AddressNormalizer.normalize(owner.getAddress());
    String householdId = householdId(lastName, address);
    owner.setHouseholdId(householdId);
    for (Owner existing : ownerRepository.findAll()) {
        if (lastName.equals(normalize(existing.getLastName()))
                && address.equals(AddressNormalizer.normalize(existing.getAddress()))
                && !householdId.equals(existing.getHouseholdId())) {
            existing.setHouseholdId(householdId);
            ownerRepository.save(existing);
        }
    }
}
private static String householdId(String lastName, String address) {
    try {
        byte[] digest = MessageDigest.getInstance("SHA-256")
                .digest((lastName + "|" + address).getBytes(StandardCharsets.UTF_8));
        StringBuilder sb = new StringBuilder(32);
        for (byte b : digest) {
            sb.append(String.format("%02x", b));
        }
        return sb.substring(0, 16).toUpperCase(Locale.ROOT);
    }
    catch (NoSuchAlgorithmException e) {
        throw new IllegalStateException("SHA-256 not available", e);
    }
}
```

